# Subagent model policy

When launching subagents (Task tool, background agents, research runners, etc.):

- **Do not** select Claude or ChatGPT/GPT family models by default.
- Prefer the session default model, or non-Claude/non-GPT options available in this environment (e.g. Composer, Grok).
- **Allowed without asking** only when the user explicitly names Claude or ChatGPT/GPT for that run.
- If a task appears to *require* Claude or ChatGPT/GPT (tooling/model capability gap), **stop and get approval** before launching with that model. Explain why in one or two sentences.

```text
❌ BAD: Task(model: "claude-…") or Task(model: "gpt-…") without user request/approval
✅ GOOD: Task() with default model, or Task(model: "…") only after explicit user instruction/approval
```
